# mem_guard_pbunion_mutant.sby -- a POSITIVE CONTROL for the owner's completion
# ruling of 2026-09-22, ITEM 4 (GEOM.PARAMBUF). INVERTED POLARITY:
# `expect fail`. It runs the SAME harness as mem_guard_no_escape.sby against
# tests/mutants/zhao_mem_guard_pbunion_mutant.sv -- a copy of the guard with
# the three region containment tests collapsed into their UNION, so a burst spanning the view0/view1 seam or running off a view into the shared scratch is admitted --
# and it PASSES only when the no-escape proof FAILS on that copy.
#
# Item 4: "Extend mem_guard_no_escape to the new authorized map; do not remove
# assertions or add assumptions that prevent illegal requests from being
# tested... Include a deliberate fault that defeats a required protection and
# makes the test/proof fail." This file is one of the two faults. Without
# them the new a1_pb_* theorems and the widened a1_region arm would be
# assertions nobody had watched fire, and a detector that has not been seen to
# fire is a claim, not an instrument.
#
# The seam is a plain `ifdef selecting the module name in formal_mem_guard.sv
# (ZHAO_GUARD_PBUNION_MUT), on the SAME `elsif chain as the other three so no run
# can define two and silently measure only the first. The production proof
# leaves it undefined; that run passing while this one fails is the pair that
# shows the selector engaged -- CLAUDE.md's negative control for a
# macro-selected mutant, and the reason the seam is an object-like `ifdef and
# not a function-like `define a -D cannot reach.
# Run with cwd = tests/formal.

[options]
mode bmc
depth 30
expect fail

[engines]
smtbmc boolector

[script]
read_slang -D ZHAO_GUARD_PBUNION_MUT --top formal_mem_guard zhao_abi_pkg.sv zhao_pkg.sv zhao_sdram_params_pkg.sv zhao_mem_guard_pbunion_mutant.sv formal_mem_guard.sv
prep -top formal_mem_guard

[files]
../../fpga/rtl/generated/zhao_abi_pkg.sv
../../fpga/rtl/common/zhao_pkg.sv
../../fpga/rtl/memory/zhao_sdram_params_pkg.sv
../../tests/mutants/zhao_mem_guard_pbunion_mutant.sv
formal_mem_guard.sv
